# unreal-mcp-cubeless Project Binding

> Legacy binding: use this file only when the task explicitly targets the external `unreal-mcp-cubeless` repository. For this repository, use `projects/UnrealMCP5_6_1.md`.

## Workspace Scope

- Default repository: `unreal-mcp-cubeless`.
- Primary consuming project for current work: `../CubelessStylized`.
- Resolve these paths relative to the discovered repository parent first.
- Keep Git status, staging, commits, pushes, and summaries separate from consuming projects and Unreal plugin submodules.

## Branch And Remote Model

- Cubeless integration/default branch: `main`.
- Cubeless fork remote: `origin` -> `https://github.com/cubeless2-lgtm/unreal-mcp-cubeless.git`.
- Original upstream remote: `upstream` -> `https://github.com/chongdashu/unreal-mcp.git`.
- `upstream` is fetch-only for routine work; do not push to upstream.
- Legacy/local extension branch: `local/pcg-tools`. Keep it unless the user explicitly asks to delete, repoint, or resync it.

## Current Engine Target

- Current target engine: Unreal Engine 5.6.1 installed at `C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6`.
- `MCPGameProject/MCPGameProject.uproject` should use `EngineAssociation` `5.6`; its Target.cs files should use UE 5.6 compatible build settings/include order.
- Keep every PCG plugin shipped with UE_5.6 enabled in `MCPGameProject`: `PCG`, `PCGBiomeCore`, `PCGBiomeSample`, `PCGExternalDataInterop`, `PCGGeometryScriptInterop`, `PCGInstancedActorsInterop`, `PCGNiagaraInterop`, and `PCGWaterInterop`.
- Preserve UE 5.6 compatibility guards for APIs introduced or changed in UE 5.7: material resource shader lookup, PCG pin current-type reporting, Niagara default-binding and enabled-renderer helpers, static mesh render LOD export, Nanite settings accessors, ControlRig blueprint headers, animation transition settings, and BlendSpace sample single-frame fields.
- When UE 5.7-only data cannot be read under UE 5.6.1, return a stable fallback value plus an `unavailable_in_ue_5_6` note instead of removing the JSON key.

## Maintenance Rule

- Do not rewrite upstream files broadly. Keep Cubeless extensions isolated and easy to review.
- For upstream update requests such as `최신 업데이트`, `업데이트 풀`, `원본 pull`, `upstream 최신`, or equivalent wording, apply `docs/workflows/mcp-upstream-update.md`.
- Preferred helper from the MCP repository root:

```powershell
.\scripts\update_with_pcg_extension.ps1
```

## MCP Agent Roles

- Planning and impact review: `agents/ieta.md`.
- MCP implementation: `agents/tivret-mcp.md`.
- Upstream synchronization: `agents/mcp-upstream-manager.md`.
- Release verification: `agents/mcp-release-verifier.md`.
- Unreal C++ review, when bridge/plugin C++ changes are involved: `agents/unreal-cpp-reviewer.md`.

## Important Local Extension Files

- `Docs/LOCAL_PCG_EXTENSION.md`
- `Docs/Tools/pcg_tools.md`
- `Docs/Tools/ai_texture_tools.md`
- `Python/tools/python_tools.py`
- `Python/tools/pcg_tools.py`
- `Python/tools/texture_generation.py`
- `Python/services/openai_image_service.py`
- `Python/services/unreal_texture_importer.py`
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/Commands/UnrealMCPProjectCommands.cpp`
- `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/UnrealMCPBridge.cpp`

## Verification

- For Python changes, run:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python -m py_compile unreal_mcp_server.py tools\python_tools.py tools\pcg_tools.py
uv --directory .\Python run python -c "import unreal_mcp_server; print('server import ok')"
```

- For AI texture tool changes, include:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python -m py_compile unreal_mcp_server.py tools\texture_generation.py services\openai_image_service.py services\unreal_texture_importer.py
```

- C++ plugin verification should use the current target engine at `C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.6` unless the user explicitly changes the target.
- Avoid kicking off a full source-engine rebuild unless necessary or explicitly requested.
